  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "cr8raOdx4C6T31pFp1FriY5AFDE=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:58.406Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Synpulse is a Zurich management consultancy serving banks and insurers, and the record singles out one structural fact: it is Flowable-exclusive, not a Camunda partner. In a sweep where dual certification is common \u2014 adesso, XTi, ELCA, GFT and Onepoint all hold both \u2014 exclusivity is the exception worth recording.\n\nSingle-platform commitment changes the conversation in a concrete way. A dual-certified firm has two vendor relationships to protect and will weigh any new layer against both alliance frameworks. An exclusive partner has one orchestration story, so a component that strengthens that story has no competing internal claim on it, and the firm's own positioning improves when the platform's weakest point is covered.\n\nThe qualifier is the firm's category: management consultancy. Like Eraneos in the same sweep, its deliverable is advice and programme design rather than running software, so it may recommend and specify a record layer without being the party that builds and operates it. That is a question to settle before a pitch, and it is why the row sits at priority 3 despite the clean platform position. Provenance: Flowable Partner Finder, mined 2026-08-18, not imprint-swept.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Synpulse (CH Zurich) \u2014 synpulse.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Management consultancy for banks/insurers. Flowable-exclusive (not a Camunda partner) \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:32:58.406503Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:58.406507Z"
    }
  },
